hadiths[26]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16644","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to me that his father informed him that a man sneezed near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah have mercy on you. Then he sneezed a second or third time, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has a cold."
"16645","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ikrimah, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to me, from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man eating with his left hand and said: Eat with your right hand. He said: I cannot. He said: May you not be able. He said: And it did not reach his mouth after that."
"16646","He said: Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Abu Umays narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from his father, he said: A spy for the polytheists came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When he ate, he slipped away. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Against the man, kill him. He said: The people raced to him. My father used to outrun the horse in sprinting. He said: He outran them to him. He said: He seized the bridle of his she-camel or its halter. He said: Then he killed him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his spoils."
"16647","He said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Maghrib at the hour the sun set, when its edge disappeared."
"16648","He said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, he said: I said to Salamah ibn al-Akwa: Upon what did you pledge to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah. He said: We pledged to him upon death."
"16649","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard al-Hasan ibn Muhammad narrating from Jabir ibn Abdullah and Salamah ibn al-Akwa, they both said: The crier of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and called: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has permitted you, so enjoy yourselves, meaning mutah of women."
"16650","He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Zuhayr, and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, he said: I used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I never saw him pray after Asr nor after Subh at all."
"16651","He said: Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, from his father, he said: We raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Hawazin and Ghatfan, and while we were thus, a man came on a red camel. He pulled something from behind the camel's saddle and hobbled the camel with it, then came walking until he sat with us eating lunch. He said: He looked at the people, and their mounts were few and most of them on foot. When he looked at the people, he went out running. He said: He came to his camel and sat upon it. He said: He went out galloping it, and he was a scout for the disbelievers. A man from us from Aslam followed him on a gray she-camel of his. Iyas said: My father said: I followed him running on my feet. He said: The head of the she-camel was at the haunch of the camel. He said: I caught up with him and was at the haunch of the she-camel, and advanced until I was at the haunch of the camel. Then I advanced until I seized the bridle of the camel and said to him: Kneel. When the camel placed its knee on the ground, I drew my sword and struck his head, and it fell off. Then I came with his mount leading it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me with the people. He said: Who killed this man. They said: Ibn al-Akwa. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All his spoils are his."
"16652","He said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, to Fazarah, and I went out with him until when we drew near the water, Abu Bakr rested late at night until when we prayed the dawn prayer he ordered us and we launched the raid. We came to the water, and Abu Bakr killed those he killed, and we were with him. Salamah said: I saw a group of people among them offspring, and I feared they would beat me to the mountain, so I caught them and shot an arrow between them and the mountain. When they saw the arrow, they stood, and there was a woman from Fazarah wearing a cloak of leather, with a daughter from the finest of the Arabs. I came driving them to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr gave me her daughter as extra spoils. I did not uncover her garment until I arrived at Madinah, then she spent the night with me and I did not uncover her garment until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me in the market and said: O Salamah, give me the woman. He said: O Messenger of Allah, she pleased me, and I have not uncovered her garment. He said: He fell silent until on the next day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met me in the market, and I had not uncovered her garment, and said: O Salamah, give me the woman, may your father be bereft of you. He said: I said: She is yours, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent her to the people of Makkah, and ransomed with her captives from the Muslims who were in the hands of the polytheists."
"16653","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to me, he said: My father informed me, he said: My uncle duelled Marhab the Jew on the day of Khaybar. Marhab said: Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, armed, a tried champion, when wars come blazing. My uncle Amir said: Khaybar knows that I am Amir, armed, an adventuring champion. They exchanged two blows. The sword of Marhab fell into the shield of Amir, and he went to bend low for him, and the sword returned upon his leg, cutting its inner vein, and his soul was in it. Salamah ibn al-Akwa said: I met people from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: The deed of Amir is void; he killed himself. Salamah said: I came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the deed of Amir is void. He said: Who said that. I said: People from your companions. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He who said that lied; rather he has his reward twice. When he went out to Khaybar he began chanting rajaz for the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among them was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) driving the mounts, saying: By Allah, were it not for Allah we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. Those who have transgressed against us, when they seek strife we refuse. We cannot dispense with Your bounty. Make firm the feet when we meet, and send down tranquility upon us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this. He said: Amir, O Messenger of Allah. He said: May your Lord forgive you. He said: He never sought forgiveness for a man specifically except he was martyred. When Umar ibn al-Khattab heard that, he said: O Messenger of Allah, would that you had let us enjoy Amir. He advanced and was martyred. Salamah said: Then the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Ali and said: I shall give the banner today to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, or whom Allah and His Messenger love. He said: I came with him leading him bleary-eyed. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in his eye, then gave him the banner. Marhab came out brandishing his sword, saying: Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, armed, a tried champion, when wars come blazing. Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah honor his face, said: I am the one whom my mother named Haydarah, like a lion of thickets, unsightly to behold. I repay them with the measure of al-Sandarah. He split the head of Marhab with the sword, and the conquest was at his hands."
"16654","He said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, from his father, he said: We arrived at Madinah at the time of al-Hudaybiyah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I and Rabah, the boy of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), went out with the camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I went out with a horse belonging to Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, intending to graze it with the camels. At dawn, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uyaynah raided the camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), killed its herdsman, and went driving them away, he and people with him on horses. I said: O Rabah, sit upon this horse, join it to Talhah, and inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that his grazing camels were raided. He said: I stood upon a hill, faced toward Madinah, then called three times: O morning attack. Then I followed the people with my sword and arrows. I began shooting at them and hamstringing them, while there were many trees. When a horseman returned toward me, I sat for him at the root of a tree, then shot. No horseman came toward me except I hamstrung him. I began shooting at them, saying: I am Ibn al-Akwa, and today is the day of al-Rudda. I would catch a man among them and shoot him while he was on his mount, and my arrow would fall in the saddle until I pierced his shoulder. I said: Take it, and I am Ibn al-Akwa, and today is the day of al-Rudda. When I was among the trees, I burned them with arrows. When the passes narrowed, I climbed the mountain and pelted them with stones. That remained my affair and theirs; I pursued them chanting rajaz until nothing Allah created of the camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained except I left it behind my back and rescued it from their hands. I kept shooting at them until they cast more than thirty spears and more than thirty cloaks, lightening themselves of them, and they cast nothing of that except I placed stones upon it and gathered upon the road of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When forenoon extended, Uyaynah ibn Badr al-Fazari came to them as reinforcement, while they were in a narrow pass. Then I climbed the mountain and was above them. Uyaynah said: What is this that I see. They said: We met from this man hardship; he has not left us since before dawn until now, and took everything in our hands and placed it behind his back. Uyaynah said: Were it not that he sees pursuers behind him, he would have left you. Let some of you rise to him. Four of them rose to him and climbed the mountain. When I made them hear the voice, I said: Do you know me. They said: Who are you. I said: I am Ibn al-Akwa, and by the One who honored the face of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), no man among you seeks me and overtakes me, nor do I seek him and he escapes me. A man among them said: I think so. He said: I did not leave that seat of mine until I saw the horsemen of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threading through the trees, and the first of them was al-Akhram al-Asadi, and after him Abu Qatadah, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and after Abu Qatadah al-Miqdad al-Kindi. The polytheists turned fleeing, and I descended from the mountain and confronted al-Akhram and seized the bridle of his horse. I said: O Akhram, warn the people, meaning beware of them, for I do not trust they will not cut you off. Wait until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions catch up. He said: O Salamah, if you believe in Allah and the Last Day, and know that Paradise is true and the Fire is true, do not stand between me and martyrdom. He said: I let go the bridle of his horse. He caught Abd al-Rahman ibn Uyaynah, and Abd al-Rahman turned upon him, and they exchanged two thrusts. Al-Akhram hamstrung Abd al-Rahman, and Abd al-Rahman thrust him and killed him. Abd al-Rahman moved from the horse of al-Akhram, and Abu Qatadah caught Abd al-Rahman, and they exchanged two thrusts. He hamstrung Abu Qatadah, and Abu Qatadah killed him. Abu Qatadah moved onto the horse of al-Akhram. Then I went out running after the people until I saw nothing of the dust of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They turned before sunset toward a ravine with water called Dhu Qarad, intending to drink from it. They saw me running behind them, turned from it, and hastened in the pass, the pass of Dhi Bir. The sun set, and I caught a man and shot him. I said: Take it, and I am Ibn al-Akwa, and today is the day of al-Rudda. He said: O bereavement of Umm Akwa for Bakrah. I said: Yes, O enemy of himself. The one I shot was Bakrah. I followed him with another arrow, and two arrows stuck in him. They left two horses, and I came with them driving them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was at the water from which I had cleared them, Dhu Qarad. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with five hundred, and Bilal had slaughtered a camel from what I left, roasting for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from its liver and hump. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, let me choose a hundred from your companions, and I shall fall upon the disbelievers by night, and none of them bearing news shall remain except I kill him. He said: Would you do that, O Salamah. He said: Yes, by the One who honored you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until I saw his molars in the light of the fire. Then he said: They are now being entertained in the land of Ghatfan. A man from Ghatfan came and said: They passed by so-and-so al-Ghatfani, and he slaughtered a camel for them. He said: When they took to skinning its hide, they saw dust and left it and fled. In the morning, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of our horsemen today is Abu Qatadah, and the best of our footmen is Salamah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the share of footman and horseman together. Then he mounted me behind him on al-Adba returning to Madinah. When we were near it about forenoon, and among the people was a man from the Ansar who was never outrun, he began calling: Is there a racer, is there no man to race to Madinah. He repeated that times, while I was behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he having mounted me behind. I said to him: Do you not honor a noble nor fear a notable. He said: No, except the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be for you, let me race the man. He said: If you wish. I said: Go to him. He leapt from his mount, and I bent my legs and leapt from the she-camel. Then I held back a mile or two, meaning I conserved myself. Then I ran until I caught him and struck between his shoulders with my hands. I said: I beat you, by Allah, or a word like it. He said: He laughed and said: I think so, until we arrived at Madinah."
"16655","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utbah Abu Yahya, judge of al-Yamamah, narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When the prayer and the supper are present, begin with the supper."
"16656","He said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever draws the sword against us is not from us."
"16657","Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Yazid, from Salamah that he used to seek the place of the mushaf, and mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek that place, and between the minbar and the qiblah was the passage of a sheep."
"16658","He said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Yazid, from Salamah, he said: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seven expeditions. He mentioned al-Hudaybiyah, the day of Hunayn, the day of al-Qarad, and the day of Khaybar. Yazid said: I forgot the rest of them."
"16659","He said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ubayd, from Salamah, he said: My uncle Amir came to me and said: Give me your weapon. He said: I gave it to him. He said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, grant me your weapon. He said: Where is your weapon. He said: I said: I gave it to my uncle Amir. He said: I find no likeness for you except the one who said: Grant me a brother more beloved to me than myself. He said: He gave me his bow, his shield, and three arrows from his quiver."
"16660","He said: Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Yazid, from Salamah that he sought permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the desert life, and he permitted him."
"16661","He said: Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn al-Harith informed us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa informed us, and Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, he said: Yala narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah narrated to me, from his father, he said: We used to pray Friday with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return while the walls had no shade in which to seek shade."
"16662","Ishaq ibn Isa and Yunus, and this is the hadith of Ishaq, said: Attaf ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, Yunus said: Ibn Abi Rabiah, he said: I heard Salamah ibn al-Akwa, and when he stopped he would stop with my father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am in hunting with nothing on me but a shirt; shall I pray in it. He said: Button it, even if you find only a thorn."
"16663","He said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Rashid al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa al-Aslami narrated to us, from his father, he said: I never heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) begin a supplication except he began it with: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, the Exalted, the Bestower. Salamah said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among those who pledged under the tree, then I passed by him after that with people with him. He said: Pledge, O Salamah. I said: I have done. He said: And also. I pledged to him the second time."
"16664","He said: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then moved to the shade of a tree. When the people lightened from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Ibn al-Akwa, will you not pledge. I said: I have pledged, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And also. He said: I pledged to him the second time. Yazid said: I said: O Abu Muslim, upon what did you pledge that day. He said: Upon death."
"16665","He said: Makki narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, he said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when it was veiled by the veil."
"16666","He said: Yunus narrated to us, he said: al-Attaf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, my father said, and other than Yunus ibn Razin said that he stopped at al-Rabadhah, he and his companions, intending Hajj. It was said to them: Here is Salamah ibn al-Akwa, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We came to him and greeted him, then asked him. He said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine, and he brought out for us his palm, a huge palm. He said: We stood to him and kissed both his palms together."
"16667","He said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abu Umays narrated to us, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted mutah of women in the year of Awtas for three days, then forbade it."
"16668","Yahya ibn Ghaylan said, he said: al-Mufaddal, meaning Ibn Fadalah, narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Said ibn Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa that his father narrated to him that Salamah arrived at Madinah, and Buraydah ibn al-Hasib met him and said: Have you apostatized from your emigration, O Salamah. He said: Allah forbid; I am with permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Begin the desert life, O Aslam, breathe the winds and dwell in the ravines. They said: We fear, O Messenger of Allah, that will harm us in our emigration. He said: You are emigrants wherever you are."
"16669","He said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from Yazid, mawla of Salamah ibn al-Akwa, from Salamah ibn al-Akwa, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah. He said: You are the people of our desert, and we are the people of your settled land."
